{
 "id": "catalogs-and-indexes",
 "title": "Catalogs, encyclopedias and machine-readable indexes of languages",
 "description": "Where to look a language up: language databases and encyclopedias (PLDB, hopl.info, FOLDOC, Wikidata, esolangs.org, Wikipedia list pages with per-section anchors of \"List of programming languages by type\"), the language registries embedded in tooling (GitHub Linguist languages.yml, Pygments/Rouge/highlight.js/Prism/Shiki lists, tree-sitter parser lists, ANTLR grammars-v4, Language Server and Debug Adapter implementor lists), online interpreters for hundreds of languages, and awesome lists. Level 0 entries are the machine-readable sources; the rest are level 3 catalogs.",
